;; dougaka — 動画家. Three roles, and the unit they share is the DESIGN FILE.
;;
;; A dougaka work order is one `videos/<slug>.edn` in
;; cloud-itonami/ai-gftd-dougaka-actor. The nightly loop
;; (kotoba-lang/loop-ka-production, channel :dougaka) drains that directory in
;; running order: each design goes through the DougakaGovernor
;; (`dougaka.produce --from`), then the engine (cloud-itonami/ai-gftd-dougaka
;; `dougaka.pipeline`) which writes a vertical mp4 + SRT + `legs.edn`, and the
;; loop grades the legs before anything is announced. Nothing in this chain
;; needs a person except the approval card on the planner's commit and the
;; :content.publish voice on the steward.
;;
;; So the Bots are the producers, and the split follows the three verbs a
;; topic passes through:
;;
;;   episode-planner  topic  -> design file       (patch.create, autonomous)
;;   qa               design -> governor bounds   (release.block, autonomous)
;;   work-catalog     host + what a "work" is     (unchanged from 2026-08-19)
;;
;; Why not one steward per work: there are still no PUBLISHED works. The ten
;; designs in videos/ are work orders, and the rendered cuts so far graded
;; :degraded (placeholder images, no bed) because no generation token reached
;; the engine — so a bot per design would again count unpublished fixtures.
;;
;; MEASURED 2026-08-22: the chain ran end to end on videos/neko-no-michi.edn
;; from a clean worktree — 60.04 s, 720x1280, h264/aac, 8 shots, legs.edn
;; {:video [:placeholder ×8] :voice [:local ×8] :bed false}; loop-ka `record`
;; graded it DEGRADED and returned exit 10 (hold). That is the loop doing its
;; job, and it is also the gap the planner cannot close: a design is only as
;; good as the legs the fleet can run for it.
;;
;; dougaka.gftd.ai was still dark on 2026-08-19 (curl exit 000). The steward
;; keeps restoration as its first bounded outcome; the planner and qa do not
;; wait on it — the publish surface is aozora.app/videos, not that host.

[{:yakuwari/id :dougaka/episode-planner
  :yakuwari/business :dougaka
  :yakuwari/project "cloud-itonami/ai-gftd-dougaka-actor"
  :yakuwari/objective
  "Turn ONE open topic into ONE design file the nightly loop can render.

   Read exactly two files: `topics/backlog.edn` (the backlog; pick the first
   entry whose :status is :open) and `topics/README.md` (the design schema
   and one complete example). Then write `videos/<slug>.edn` in that exact
   tx-data shape — a one-element vector holding a map with :db/id -1 and the
   :video/ namespaced keys, :video/scenes stored as a pr-str'd string — and
   commit it together with the topic's :status flipped to :designed and
   :design set to the slug. One topic, one file, one commit per tick.

   Design inside the governor's bounds or the loop will hold it: total
   duration 45–90 s (hard ceiling 120), at most 24 shots, no shot over 10 s,
   every :prompt a vertical 9:16 live-action description, no real person's
   likeness, no brand, no third-party character. Subtitles are the narration;
   one short Japanese line per shot.

   If backlog.edn has no :open entry, do nothing and say so — do not invent a
   topic. If the file is missing, report that as the finding. The commit is
   a held write: it lands when approved, and you do not approve it."
  :yakuwari/scale {:min 0 :desired 1 :max 1}
  :yakuwari/runners [{:runner :claude :weight 1}]
  :bot/role :episode-planner
  :bot/name "dougaka 企画"
  :bot/cadence-minutes 1440
  :yakuwari/capabilities
  [{:capability :metrics.read :decision :autonomous}
   {:capability :patch.create :decision :autonomous
    :note "A design file is a patch. Writing it is the job."}
   {:capability :patch.integrate :decision :approval-required
    :note "The commit is a held write; a person (or the steward's omakase, if ever set) lands it."}
   {:capability :content.publish :decision :blocked
    :note "The planner never announces. Publication is the actor's own announce leg under the loop's grant."}
   {:capability :spend.commit :decision :blocked}]}

 {:yakuwari/id :dougaka/qa
  :yakuwari/business :dougaka
  :yakuwari/project "cloud-itonami/ai-gftd-dougaka-actor"
  :yakuwari/objective
  "Try to falsify that the next design the loop will render is inside the
   DougakaGovernor's bounds, before the loop spends a night on it.

   Read `topics/backlog.edn` to find the most recently :designed slug, then
   read that `videos/<slug>.edn`. Check, and report each as a measured
   yes/no: total shot duration ≤ 120 s and inside 45–90; shots ≤ 24; every
   shot ≤ 10 s; every prompt is a vertical 9:16 live-action description;
   no real-person likeness, brand, or third-party character in any prompt or
   subtitle; :video/scenes parses as EDN. A failed check is a release block:
   record the smallest counterexample (the shot :seq and the field) and
   flip that topic back to :status :open with a :qa-note so the planner
   redoes it. A design with no failures is reported as clean — do not edit
   it. Do not grade craft; grade bounds."
  :yakuwari/scale {:min 0 :desired 1 :max 1}
  :yakuwari/runners [{:runner :claude :weight 1}]
  :bot/role :qa
  :bot/name "dougaka 検品"
  :bot/cadence-minutes 1440
  :yakuwari/capabilities
  [{:capability :metrics.read :decision :autonomous}
   {:capability :test.run :decision :autonomous}
   {:capability :release.block :decision :autonomous
    :note "Flipping a topic back to :open is the block; it is a held write like any other."}
   {:capability :issue.create :decision :autonomous}
   {:capability :patch.create :decision :autonomous}
   {:capability :patch.integrate :decision :approval-required}
   {:capability :content.publish :decision :blocked}
   {:capability :deploy.production :decision :blocked}]}

 {:yakuwari/id :dougaka/work-catalog
  :yakuwari/business :dougaka
  :yakuwari/project "cloud-itonami/ai-gftd-dougaka"
  :yakuwari/objective
  "Get dougaka to the point where it HAS works, then say what they are. Two
   bounded outcomes in order; the second does not start before the first lands.

   1. dougaka.gftd.ai did not answer on 2026-08-19 (curl exit 000, no TLS
      handshake). Establish why and propose the restoration. Report the
      measured status code every run: 000, a 5xx, and a 200 serving an empty
      catalog are three different failures and only the last is about content.

   2. Once it answers, decide what a dougaka work IS. Since 2026-08-22 the
      production unit is settled upstream of you: one `videos/<slug>.edn`
      design in ai-gftd-dougaka-actor, rendered by the nightly loop, graded
      by its legs. A WORK is a design whose cut graded :clean and was
      announced. Count those — if the answer is zero, say zero — and say
      which, if any, of the five internal examples in this repo should
      become one.

   Meanwhile do not call the examples a catalog. They are renderer fixtures,
   and calling them works reports a product no reader can reach."
  :yakuwari/scale {:min 0 :desired 1 :max 1}
  :yakuwari/runners [{:runner :claude :weight 1}]
  :bot/role :work-steward
  :bot/name "dougaka catalog"
  :bot/cadence-minutes 1440
  :yakuwari/capabilities
  [{:capability :metrics.read :decision :autonomous}
   {:capability :test.run :decision :autonomous}
   {:capability :issue.create :decision :autonomous}
   {:capability :patch.create :decision :autonomous}
   {:capability :content.publish :decision :voice-required}
   {:capability :patch.integrate :decision :approval-required}
   {:capability :deploy.production :decision :approval-required
    :note "Restoring the host is a production deploy. Propose it; a person lands it."}]}]
